From b9dd8827f87116a66161624b14f69c227cead9df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gervais <lab@aurora-lab.local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:35:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(artifacts): explain truncated write_artifact calls
 instead of looping

When a write_artifact call is cut off by the model's output-token limit
(Bedrock Converse defaults to 4096 since no max_tokens is set), the args
arrive as {"title": ...} or {}. The pydantic args schema rejected these
inside the ToolNode before the tool function ran, so the model only saw
"content: Field required" and retried the same oversized document, and
each attempt left an execution_steps row stuck in 'running' (the capture
wrapper never ran).

Register the tool with the equivalent plain JSON schema (content still
required in what the model sees) so the call reaches write_artifact,
which now returns an error naming the likely truncation and asking for a
shorter document. The step is closed as an error by the capture wrapper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
